      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This abstract reports a single study that tested a path model linking early positive memories to eating psychopathology via social safeness and body appreciation. The path analysis was conducted in a sample of 490 women and the model explained 51% of variance; social safeness and body appreciation mediated the effect of early warmth memories on disordered eating, controlling for BMI. No information on country, age, ethnicity, BMI mean, assessment instruments, or survey method is provided.",
